WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.220
- Let's give it up for
Daughtry's lead singer,

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.053
Chris Daughtry!

00:00:03.053 --> 00:00:06.660
(rock music playing)
(audience applauding)

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.493
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:07.493 --> 00:00:08.570
Hey, what's up, man?

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.491
Your beard game is on point.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.510
(Chris laughs)

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.343
- Thank you so much.

00:00:13.343 --> 00:00:14.370
Good to see you.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.203
Oh, my God.

00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:16.450
You guys are having
way too much fun there.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.490
I wish I was there.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.250
- I know, I might've had too much macha.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.834
I know I have a lot of caffeine.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.650
(laughing)
So something's happening.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.990
- I got my coffee here.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.720
It's my drug of choice these days.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:26.553
- It's my lifeline.

00:00:26.553 --> 00:00:27.386
I love it.

00:00:27.386 --> 00:00:28.950
How have you been?
- Yeah.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:30.283
I'm awesome.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.800
Honestly, like, life is so good.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.090
I miss being on the road,

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.100
but, I'm also really
loving this home life.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.060
I haven't been home this long
in 15 years, so, it's cool.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:45.260
I get to be on your show and
at home at the same time.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.130
- I know, it's like, says every musician

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.760
in the world for the last year and a half.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.210
Like every, everybody just
was like, "Wait, what?

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.043
What do we do?"

00:00:52.043 --> 00:00:53.096
Like, 'cause we're all
used to going and going.

00:00:53.096 --> 00:00:54.610
- Yeah, it takes some getting used to.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.580
- Yeah, agreed.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.660
Well, your new song is
called "Heavy Is The Crown."

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.660
So, what's it about?

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:02.550
- You know, I think, I was
thinking about it today.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.130
I was like, "We're all kind of, like,

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.770
the stars of our own movie."

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:07.603
You know what I mean?

00:01:07.603 --> 00:01:10.360
Like, we're all are, are all
the leads in our own film

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.780
and we're, we are the kings
and queens of our own castle.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:19.780
And life has so much, like,
there's so much pressure on

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.320
just to live, especially these days.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.590
And, not only that, but the pressures of

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:27.850
carving your own path

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:31.420
without conforming to what
everyone else thinks is normal.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:32.840
And...

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:37.840
Yeah, just the daily choices
that we have to make.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.840
It's a lot of pressure sometimes.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.060
And, I guess you can
kinda sum it up that way.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.100
- Yeah, I mean, God, that was nicely done.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.120
I feel a little sad, but that's okay.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.420
Performing...
(laughing)

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.910
'Cause I love the message.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:52.840
I love that it's deep.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.290
And I think a lot of people relate

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:56.020
especially for this past year and a half.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.730
Everybody, you know, heavy is a crown.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.240
You feel, if you're
responsible for your family,

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.420
if your responsible for...

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.200
There's, you know, a lot
going on, financial crisis,

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.700
mental health is an issue right now,

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.790
people have lost their jobs.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.650
Like, it's a lot going on.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.400
So, it's, you know, probably
good to have a song that,

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.253
you know, comes out and people relate to.

